  "notes": [
    "Captured as source text only for task M4-T036 (D-090 R291, R517, R526; backlog DB-188): the Zoning Resolution texts the two independent step-P5 readings named as not had. The capture holds the official source text and its provenance; it encodes no rule, no reading of the text for any lot, and no number derived from it.",
    "Channel: the authoritative, sha256-and-byte-pinned channel is the canonical section HTML (raw_html_sha256 and response_bytes in source). The section's own print/PDF render was fetched once and used ONLY as a text check; per M4-T025 finding F4 (DB-167) the PDF bytes are regenerated per request and are NOT pinned.",
    "Further sections this text points to that are NOT captured by this snapshot: 32-10.",
    "PDF text-check is PARTIAL for this section: pdftotext does not reproduce 200 styled table-cell word(s) and 0 prose word(s) (styled cells / line-wraps); those are present in the sha256-pinned HTML (the authoritative channel) - the prose verbatim and every table cell are captured from the HTML. See cross_check.result.",
    "The Use Group tables carry a PRC (Parking Requirement Category) column and NO loading requirement category column. The PRC letter-to-ratio parking tables are in the existing capture zr-36-21 and the required loading berths are in the existing capture zr-36-62 (neither re-fetched here). Captured cell-by-cell from the authoritative HTML; the styled permission symbols are not reliably extracted by pdftotext (cross-check partial).",
    "The pinned raw_html_sha256 and response_bytes are of THIS session's fetch of the whole page. The page's non-body chrome carries a per-render Drupal form token (form_build_id) in the site search form, so the whole-page digest can differ between sessions while the section body is byte-stable; the reproducible semantic pin is content_digest_sha256 over verbatim_excerpt (the stdlib extractor reproduces the committed zr-35-31 capture's verbatim_excerpt byte-for-byte).",
    "Nothing in this record is a Verified zoning determination (ADR-007: a rule citing it ships under the standing not-professionally-reviewed label with a direct source link; professional review is advisory)."
